WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.499
JAMIE: Right, but "up to seventy-five
percent" is a vendor benchmark.
RapidCanvas is

00:00:04.499 --> 00:00:08.998
JAMIE: the one saying it. There's no
independent evaluation in the Axios
piece.

00:00:09.108 --> 00:00:12.815
ALEX: Fair. But even if the real number
is half that—

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.483
JAMIE: Then someone at the company still
has to figure out which half

00:00:14.483 --> 00:00:16.126
JAMIE: was wrong.

00:00:16.236 --> 00:00:19.753
RUFUS: The "no-code" framing is what
interests me. Every time a tool markets

00:00:19.753 --> 00:00:23.271
RUFUS: itself as no-code, what it's
actually selling is: the complexity
still exists,

00:00:23.271 --> 00:00:26.788
RUFUS: you just don't see it.
